# core.rk — thin Rusk names for the native `simple` GUI primaries.
#
# Every window is a number, every control is a number, and every event is a
# piece of text. The higher modules in this folder build on these names; they
# never speak directly to the operating system. A program on a non-Windows
# target still checks and bakes: these primaries become safe no-ops there.

# A new window. It is hidden until `simple_window_show` is called.
to simple_window_new with title as view of text and width as a number and height as a number:
    give back make simple window titled title wide width high height

to simple_window_show with window as a number:
    show simple window window

to simple_window_close:
    close simple window

to simple_button_new with window as a number and text as view of text and x as a number and y as a number and width as a number and height as a number:
    give back add simple button to window labelled text at x and y sized width and height

to simple_label_new with window as a number and text as view of text and x as a number and y as a number and width as a number and height as a number:
    give back add simple label to window labelled text at x and y sized width and height

to simple_field_new with window as a number and text as view of text and x as a number and y as a number and width as a number and height as a number:
    give back add simple field to window labelled text at x and y sized width and height

to simple_control_set_text with control as a number and text as view of text:
    set simple text of control to text

to simple_control_text with control as a number:
    give back simple text of control

to simple_events_pump:
    pump simple events

to simple_event_next:
    give back next simple event

to simple_event_control:
    give back simple event control

to simple_confirm with text as view of text:
    give back simple confirm with text

to simple_message with text as view of text:
    show simple message text
